    "details": {
      "description": "<p>Hidden in the stonework, a draconic maw of earth waits to consume its next victim. </p>",
      "disable": "<p>@Check[arcana|dc:28|traits:action:disable-a-device]{Arcana}, @Check[nature|dc:28|traits:action:disable-a-device]{Nature}, @Check[religion|dc:28|traits:action:disable-a-device]{Religion}, @Check[occultism|dc:28|traits:action:disable-a-device]{Occultism}, or @Check[thievery|dc:28|traits:action:disable-a-device]{Thievery} to banish the primal magics animating the stonework.</p>",
      "isComplex": false,
      "level": {
        "value": 8
      },
      "publication": {
        "authors": "",
        "license": "OGL",
        "remaster": false,
        "title": "Covalon: Whitespire Expedition"
      },
      "reset": "<p>1 day. Upon a successful disable check or reaching its broken threshold, the jaws meld back into the stonework, leaving no sign of their presence.</p><p>If a creature Escapes but the hazard is still active, Consume can be triggered again if a creature moves within its Jaws range. This cannot trigger in the same turn as a creature escapes the jaws. </p>",
